1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Eleventh Episode
The Spirit of Sleep
Sleeping Spirit

15
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:44,500
Let's play!

16
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,560
Okay!

17
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:48,940
Let's go!

18
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:50,600
Your Highness!

19
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,580
Good morning.

20
00:02:55,563 --> 00:02:57,179
Why are you sneaking around?

21
00:02:57,204 --> 00:02:58,760
Today is a day where it's okay to play.

22
00:02:59,524 --> 00:03:00,839
Ah, that's right!

23
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:02,606
Whoa, I'm flying!

24
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:06,500
However, you must not get carried away just because you are away from your parents.

25
00:03:06,624 --> 00:03:09,060
You haven't forgotten your promise to your mother, have you?

26
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:10,200
Rule one!

27
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,133
Keep track of time at the mountain lodge!

28
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,280
And then?

29
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,740
Rule one!

30
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:20,733
Since I get into fights easily, I must practice not getting angry during this one-week break!

31
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:22,120
You understand, right?

32
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,340
Alright, I'm going off to play!

33
00:03:23,584 --> 00:03:24,584
Opal!

34
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:30,860
Good grief...

35
00:03:30,884 --> 00:03:33,523
Help me!

36
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,286
Garigori, where has the Prince gone?

37
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,240
What? It's just Dr. Uranari!

38
00:03:39,264 --> 00:03:40,810
It is not time yet, I tell you!

39
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,540
Time doesn't matter!

40
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:43,880
He’s a Prince, a young Prince!

41
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,824
The Prince—er, His Highness—

42
00:03:45,848 --> 00:03:49,440
is playing on the hill, but... the time... I mean, the schedule must be kept!

43
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,660
Wow!

44
00:04:03,709 --> 00:04:04,740
Beautiful scenery!

45
00:04:05,026 --> 00:04:05,406
Yeah!

46
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:13,339
That's the King's chair, right?

47
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,260
Yeah, it's the King's...

48
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:18,959
I wonder what's about to start?

49
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:21,420
Your Highness!

50
00:04:23,105 --> 00:04:25,820
Your Highness, please return to the mountain lodge immediately!

51
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:26,480
No way!

52
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,680
I'm right in the middle of playing!

53
00:04:27,910 --> 00:04:30,160
Don't be ridiculous, go on now!

54
00:04:35,166 --> 00:04:37,606
No, no, I don't want to!

55
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,700
What’s the point of wearing a thing like this!?

56
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:43,576
The King is ill, so you must deliver the welcoming address in his stead...

57
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,420
Well? Who?

58
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,600
His Highness Plastic.

59
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,440
Plastic?

60
00:04:46,794 --> 00:04:48,286
Huh, Duralumin's kid?

61
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:50,576
Indeed, that little pest...

62
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,553
If Lord Duralumin hears that, it'll be a disaster!

63
00:04:54,090 --> 00:04:57,900
I mean, did it really take him 8 years to finally graduate from kindergarten?

64
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:00,980
It took him 8 years to graduate from kindergarten?

65
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:04,180
Please, keep it down.

66
00:05:05,995 --> 00:05:09,506
Grand Duke Duralumin has arrived!

67
00:05:28,805 --> 00:05:31,905
Oh, Plastic, it doesn't hurt, it doesn't hurt. There, you're fine.

68
00:05:31,930 --> 00:05:35,240
Now, Plastic. Give a proper greeting just like we practiced.

69
00:05:35,365 --> 00:05:38,440
Show them your best side so you don't lose to the likes of Sapphire.

70
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:41,280
Nylon, you did make him practice, didn't you?

71
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:42,163
Flawlessly.

72
00:05:43,755 --> 00:05:45,393
Yo, hello.

73
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:52,320
Prince Sapphire, I would appreciate it if you offered your greeting according to protocol.

74
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:54,833
Never mind that, never mind that. Plastic, congratulations.

75
00:05:54,945 --> 00:05:56,293
Oh, th-thanks.

76
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,680
Hey now, Plastic, give your greeting.

77
00:06:04,550 --> 00:06:05,550
Turn right.

78
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,735
What kind of practice was that?!

79
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,300
Well, even if you say that...

80
00:06:21,635 --> 00:06:22,840
What's so funny?

81
00:06:23,365 --> 00:06:25,340
Let's skip the greetings and go play.

82
00:06:25,895 --> 00:06:28,180
Forget Duralumin! Plastic, let's go play!

83
00:06:35,230 --> 00:06:38,420
When dining, do this, then that, and then—do you understand?

84
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:41,420
Drink with your spoon without making a sound.

85
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:45,860
And then do this, and it goes like this, like this, like this, like this, like this, like this...

86
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:49,719
Good grief, what a dimwit. Not worth teaching at all.

87
00:06:49,795 --> 00:06:52,406
Straighten up a bit.

88
00:06:55,855 --> 00:06:57,446
Why, you little brat...!

89
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:00,373
How dare you bite my nose...

90
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,955
Nylon, what were you doing?

91
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:11,440
Oh, nothing really, I was just astonished by how quick a learner Prince Plastic is.

92
00:07:11,665 --> 00:07:14,100
Oh, is that so? Well then, shall we go to dinner?

93
00:07:30,365 --> 00:07:32,840
A toast to celebrate Prince Plastic's graduation.

94
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,220
Cheers.

95
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:41,640
Damn it, as if I'd ever let Sapphire sit on that throne!

96
00:07:42,015 --> 00:07:43,760
Sapphire must be a woman.

97
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:46,360
By law, a woman cannot take the throne.

98
00:07:46,815 --> 00:07:50,540
Once Sapphire is taken care of, the throne will belong to Plastic.

99
00:07:52,085 --> 00:07:54,900
After all, Dad is the King's only brother.

100
00:07:55,110 --> 00:07:57,549
You are more than qualified. Let people laugh if they want—

101
00:07:57,573 --> 00:08:02,200
I will definitely make sure Plastic sits on that throne!

102
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:12,160
Plastic, where are you going?

103
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,720
I'm going too, Your Highness!

104
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:16,720
Hey, Plastic, wait up.

105
00:08:17,345 --> 00:08:20,620
Plastic! Come on, let's play, Plastic.

106
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,420
So you like pictures, huh?

107
00:08:30,125 --> 00:08:31,560
Well, that's impossible.

108
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,516
Because this is just a picture, see? You can't take it.

109
00:08:33,541 --> 00:08:34,981
I want to eat dat.

110
00:08:35,005 --> 00:08:37,780
This is called a winter strawberry—a strawberry picked in winter.

111
00:08:37,993 --> 00:08:39,333
But like I said, this is just a picture.

112
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:40,889
I want to eat dat! I want it!

113
00:08:40,913 --> 00:08:42,340
You want to eat something you can't have?!

114
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:45,256
What a handful!

115
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:46,800
I'm sorry, Plastic.

116
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,380
I already said I'm sorry.

117
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,881
I want to eat it!

118
00:08:54,905 --> 00:08:57,040
Well, that's asking for the impossible, Plastic.

119
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:59,708
It's summer right now. Winter strawberries can only be picked in winter.

120
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:00,840
I want to eat it!

121
00:09:02,226 --> 00:09:03,120
We have them, we have them!

122
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,566
There are winter strawberries!

123
00:09:04,591 --> 00:09:06,160
What? Are you saying they can be found even in summer?

124
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,080
Yes.

125
00:09:07,355 --> 00:09:10,340
Deep in these woods, there's a field where winter strawberries grow even in summer.

126
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:11,480
Go pick them.

127
00:09:12,409 --> 00:09:13,740
I've sent the soldiers to fetch them.

128
00:09:14,039 --> 00:09:15,360
However, Grand Duke Duralumin...

129
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,561
Rest assured, I've made sure everyone thinks that the selfish person

130
00:09:18,586 --> 00:09:21,920
demanding winter strawberries in the middle of the night is Prince Sapphire.

131
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,180
Hmm, well done.

132
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:32,186
It's kind of noisy.

133
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,960
The prize money is mine.

134
00:10:12,656 --> 00:10:13,231
Oh, thank goodness.

135
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,120
Who's making a racket in the middle of the night?

136
00:10:43,439 --> 00:10:44,600
Help!

137
00:10:51,529 --> 00:10:53,740
Are you surprised, you foolish human alliance?

138
00:11:02,798 --> 00:11:03,800
It's a demon!

139
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,499
Foolish humans.

140
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:12,346
Do you think that will work against the Sandman, the Spirit of Sleep?

141
00:11:12,715 --> 00:11:13,920
Spirit of Sleep.

142
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,160
Spirit of Sleep.

143
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:18,080
Anyone staying up late at night is my enemy!

144
00:11:18,395 --> 00:11:20,193
On top of that, you went and trashed the forest!

145
00:11:20,505 --> 00:11:22,114
What kind of punishment should I give you?

146
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:23,139
Endo!

147
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,260
Yes!

148
00:11:25,349 --> 00:11:26,500
Endo, hand me that!

149
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:27,960
OK!

150
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:35,821
Anger potion, crying potion, laughing potion, sleeping potion... Ah, here it is!

151
00:11:36,025 --> 00:11:37,025
Here you go, big brother!

152
00:11:38,769 --> 00:11:40,246
Now, take your punishment!

153
00:11:40,490 --> 00:11:43,940
What!?

154
00:11:48,869 --> 00:11:51,220
I'm an angel, so potions don't work on me.

155
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:56,560
Fine then, you guys can just go ahead and catch a cold like that!

156
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:57,670
Serve you right!

157
00:12:00,599 --> 00:12:03,600
Hey, who on earth brought you guys out here in the middle of the night!?

158
00:12:04,070 --> 00:12:08,780
It was Prince Sapphire. Late at night, he suddenly said he wanted to eat winter strawberries.

159
00:12:09,014 --> 00:12:10,440
Prince Sapphire!?

160
00:12:10,441 --> 00:12:11,155
Damn it!

161
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:12,180
That fool of a prince!

162
00:12:12,639 --> 00:12:14,586
Endo what kind of punishment should we give?

163
00:12:15,194 --> 00:12:16,860
You know, right?

164
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,500
Yes!

165
00:12:27,519 --> 00:12:29,160
Now then, Plastic.

166
00:12:31,329 --> 00:12:36,029
Just a little more patience. Come on, sit on the throne. Let Papa take a look at you.

167
00:12:36,053 --> 00:12:37,025
Yes

168
00:12:43,486 --> 00:12:44,460
Ouch!

169
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:45,720
Ugh, what an infuriating child!

170
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,260
When I tell you to sit, you sit!

171
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,060
Oh, Papa swears to you.

172
00:12:51,084 --> 00:12:51,897
I will make you King, no matter what!

173
00:12:51,921 --> 00:12:55,720
I will sit you in that seat and place a crown upon your head!

174
00:12:55,945 --> 00:12:59,320
Even if you're a bit lacking, I have the power!

175
00:13:03,789 --> 00:13:07,960
Don't go home early... right on time...

176
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:23,880
Hey!

177
00:13:27,539 --> 00:13:28,880
You selfish idiot prince!

178
00:13:29,181 --> 00:13:30,660
Lord Sandman has come to punish you!

179
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:31,540
Wake up!

180
00:13:33,679 --> 00:13:34,679
He's sleeping soundly!

181
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:38,060
A Sleep Fairy can't go attacking someone who's already asleep!

182
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,640
Alright!

183
00:13:39,665 --> 00:13:40,346
No!

184
00:13:41,310 --> 00:13:42,520
I am the Sleep Fairy, Lord Sandman

185
00:13:42,805 --> 00:13:44,520
I'll make it so you can never sleep again for the rest of your life!

186
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:48,420
Sleep Fairy?

187
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:49,460
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

188
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:50,780
Don't play dumb!

189
00:13:51,054 --> 00:13:53,993
Because you wanted winter strawberries, the forest is a complete mess!

190
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:55,760
Stop it!

191
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:56,880
I won't!

192
00:13:57,195 --> 00:13:59,240
I don't want any winter strawberries!

193
00:13:59,340 --> 00:13:59,895
Then who was it?

194
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,920
The one who wanted them!

195
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,360
You tell me!

196
00:14:04,685 --> 00:14:05,685
You're trying to play dumb!

197
00:14:06,193 --> 00:14:07,333
Grand Duke

198
00:14:08,579 --> 00:14:10,880
Um... the one who wanted winter strawberries was Plastic!

199
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,280
The prince isn't that stupid!

200
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,840
Don't say unnecessary things!

201
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:15,200
Plastic?

202
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,240
In that case, where is he?!

203
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:19,373
If you do something terrible to Plastic, I won't forgive you!

204
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,153
Get out of the way! Move it!

205
00:14:22,849 --> 00:14:23,849
Well then, farewell!

206
00:14:26,375 --> 00:14:27,746
You did it!

207
00:14:28,189 --> 00:14:29,600
It's the Wind Fairy!

208
00:14:35,469 --> 00:14:37,020
As if anyone could match Lord Sandman!

209
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,466
Now you've done it!

210
00:14:41,115 --> 00:14:43,400
Tobi-de yo! Hi no sei yo!

211
00:14:52,579 --> 00:14:54,840
Oh no... didn't I promise not to get angry?

212
00:15:00,386 --> 00:15:01,999
Who are you?

213
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,080
Endo!

214
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:03,500
Hey!

215
00:15:03,575 --> 00:15:05,666
Are you really going to bully someone that young?

216
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,720
I have no intention of bullying them!

217
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:12,040
This kid tried to hit me out of nowhere! When I dodged, he started throwing a fit!

218
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:14,820
Good boy, Endo!

219
00:15:17,239 --> 00:15:20,226
I'll make it so you can never sleep again!

220
00:15:24,929 --> 00:15:26,940
Bro, are you gonna go after someone dressed so nicely?

221
00:15:28,459 --> 00:15:29,986
Well, I'll let it slide!

222
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,180
Let's go, Endo!

223
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,280
Alright!

224
00:15:34,649 --> 00:15:36,499
I want to eat winter strawberries...

225
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:39,260
Here he comes!

226
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:56,386
Hey you!

227
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,513
You selfish blockhead!

228
00:15:57,810 --> 00:16:00,640
Because of your selfishness, my forest is a complete mess!

229
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,020
What's so funny?!

230
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:08,620
I'll make it so you can never sleep again!

231
00:16:17,349 --> 00:16:19,920
Plastic... what happened?

232
00:16:21,129 --> 00:16:23,200
Wow, did the winter strawberries arrive?

233
00:16:23,869 --> 00:16:24,880
Who cares about that!

234
00:16:25,055 --> 00:16:26,460
Something's wrong with Plastic!

235
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:29,200
Strange? Wasn't he already strange to begin with?

236
00:16:29,485 --> 00:16:30,140
Fool!

237
00:16:30,141 --> 00:16:31,420
I mean he’s really become strange now!

238
00:16:39,809 --> 00:16:42,180
Good grief... stupidity can only be cured by death!

239
00:16:45,169 --> 00:16:48,673
Come now, Plastic, close your eyes. Gently, close your eyes...

240
00:16:48,697 --> 00:16:52,940
You're getting sleepy, so very sleepy. It's sleepy-time! Night-night time!

241
00:17:01,075 --> 00:17:03,940
Not only are you an idiot, you’re a total blowhard!

242
00:17:05,924 --> 00:17:08,740
Oh, my Plastic...

243
00:17:09,239 --> 00:17:10,239
Plastic!

244
00:17:10,679 --> 00:17:11,880
How can I help you?

245
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,240
Duralumin, I might be able to cure him!

246
00:17:14,599 --> 00:17:15,599
Wait for me!

247
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:18,780
Opal!

248
00:17:19,309 --> 00:17:20,400
Your Highness, where are you going?

249
00:17:20,994 --> 00:17:23,319
I'm going to ask the Spirit of Sleep about Plastic!

250
00:17:24,615 --> 00:17:25,335
You must not!

251
00:17:25,359 --> 00:17:27,900
What will you do if the same thing happens to you that happened to Plastic?

252
00:17:28,229 --> 00:17:29,360
I'll be fine!

253
00:17:29,659 --> 00:17:31,560
Besides, don't you feel sorry for Plastic?

254
00:17:32,289 --> 00:17:34,220
Plastic is your enemy!

255
00:17:34,589 --> 00:17:35,573
Oh, that's right!

256
00:17:36,889 --> 00:17:39,329
That hateful son of Duralumin! He is an unforgivable enemy...

257
00:17:39,353 --> 00:17:42,500
trying to usurp your throne! We have no reason to help him!

258
00:17:42,698 --> 00:17:43,478
Idiots!

259
00:17:49,149 --> 00:17:50,520
Sandman!

260
00:17:51,294 --> 00:17:53,200
Sandman!

261
00:17:53,479 --> 00:17:55,800
Sandman! Are you looking for me?!

262
00:17:56,469 --> 00:17:58,200
Sandman!

263
00:17:58,849 --> 00:18:00,320
Where are you?!

264
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:05,800
Sandman!

265
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,840
Please, I beg you!

266
00:18:07,394 --> 00:18:09,540
What, did you come to get revenge for earlier this evening?

267
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,760
Alright, just you wait!

268
00:18:11,554 --> 00:18:12,345
That's not it!

269
00:18:12,369 --> 00:18:13,480
That's wrong, Sandman!

270
00:18:13,679 --> 00:18:15,280
How's that, pitch black, isn't it!

271
00:18:15,614 --> 00:18:17,740
I can't tell what's going on when it's bright out!

272
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:22,680
One more time!

273
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:24,960
What's wrong?

274
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:25,660
Stop it!

275
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:27,080
One more time!

276
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,340
Sandman!

277
00:18:29,939 --> 00:18:32,033
Please, you must fix Plastic!

278
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,080
No way!

279
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:34,420
Please!

280
00:18:34,564 --> 00:18:37,313
I'll apologize for ruining the forest!

281
00:18:38,169 --> 00:18:39,520
You're groveling because you're scared, aren't you?

282
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:40,400
Coward!

283
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:41,620
What did you say?!

284
00:18:43,109 --> 00:18:44,109
Oh no! I'm not supposed to fight, am I?

285
00:18:44,284 --> 00:18:46,140
Endo, do that thing to the coward!

286
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,240
Okay, Big Brother!

287
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,400
There we go!

288
00:19:03,514 --> 00:19:04,900
I fell asleep... wait, what?

289
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:06,700
Stop it!

290
00:19:06,784 --> 00:19:07,784
I told you, no!

291
00:19:09,299 --> 00:19:10,680
Who do you think you are!

292
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:11,980
Who are you!

293
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,060
Whaddya want?

294
00:19:13,084 --> 00:19:13,900
Insolent, you say?!

295
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,160
Why am I insolent?!

296
00:19:15,339 --> 00:19:17,580
I'm not insolent!

297
00:19:22,764 --> 00:19:24,380
You should just get mad if they do that!

298
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,620
This prank is going way too far!

299
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:29,480
Ah, that's fairy medicine!

300
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:31,200
Weakling!

301
00:19:31,444 --> 00:19:33,580
And to think that's supposed to be a prince!

302
00:19:36,589 --> 00:19:39,180
Here is the potion to make them angry!

303
00:19:46,709 --> 00:19:48,653
Now I'm mad!

304
00:19:50,819 --> 00:19:52,880
Now, try this next!

305
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,285
Hey, Sandman!

306
00:19:58,310 --> 00:19:59,310
Sandman's here!

307
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:00,820
Coward!

308
00:20:00,894 --> 00:20:02,300
You're just like a girl!

309
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,380
Like what?

310
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:04,226
Sandman!

311
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:05,360
That's it, now I'm mad!

312
00:20:05,425 --> 00:20:06,425
I'll take you on!

313
00:20:06,460 --> 00:20:07,119
Come on!

314
00:20:08,979 --> 00:20:09,979
Come on, what's wrong?!

315
00:20:10,024 --> 00:20:11,024
Where'd all your energy go?!

316
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:16,880
Endo, help me!

317
00:20:16,904 --> 00:20:17,920
All right!

318
00:20:27,659 --> 00:20:30,360
Now you've made me angry-!

319
00:20:34,639 --> 00:20:36,100
Like I'd ever tell you, even if you try to intimidate me!

320
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:37,520
Tell me!

321
00:20:37,899 --> 00:20:39,560
Tell me how to fix Plastic!

322
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:40,340
No way!

323
00:20:40,529 --> 00:20:41,746
He can just stay like that for the rest of his life!

324
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:42,860
Please!

325
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:44,220
Tell me!

326
00:20:45,019 --> 00:20:46,926
If I tell you, will you do as I say?

327
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:48,440
Yeah!

328
00:20:49,129 --> 00:20:51,520
Then bow down on your hands and knees in front of me and beg!

329
00:20:52,599 --> 00:20:54,060
Bow down and beg?

330
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:54,960
That's right!

331
00:20:55,069 --> 00:20:57,200
You gotta get on your hands and knees and beg!

332
00:20:58,520 --> 00:20:59,060
What's the matter?

333
00:20:59,334 --> 00:21:00,334
You can't do it, can you?

334
00:21:01,044 --> 00:21:02,980
A prince getting down on his hands and knees to beg!

335
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:05,900
Please!

336
00:21:06,059 --> 00:21:07,500
Please, tell me!

337
00:21:09,749 --> 00:21:10,820
This is priceless!

338
00:21:11,149 --> 00:21:13,400
A prince just got down on his hands and knees and begged me!

339
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,200
Look, Endo!

340
00:21:16,469 --> 00:21:17,860
And to think he's supposed to be a prince!

341
00:21:21,125 --> 00:21:22,125
Big brother!

342
00:21:22,359 --> 00:21:23,540
That's cowardly!

343
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,340
Sapphire!

344
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,580
I'll teach you a lesson!

345
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,253
You!

346
00:21:32,739 --> 00:21:33,880
You're in a different mood, aren't you!

347
00:21:34,329 --> 00:21:36,200
Going out of your way for someone else's sake!

348
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:37,740
Sandman!

349
00:21:52,914 --> 00:21:54,460
Plastic!

350
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:58,140
Plastic!

351
00:21:58,869 --> 00:21:59,869
What is that jar for?

352
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,080
If you try anything funny...!

353
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:02,033
Shut up!

354
00:22:02,215 --> 00:22:03,993
This is medicine to cure Plastic!

355
00:22:17,594 --> 00:22:20,155
Plastic is cured, thank goodness!

356
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:21,180
Thank goodness!

357
00:22:21,605 --> 00:22:22,400
Your Highness!

358
00:22:22,425 --> 00:22:24,020
I don't know how to thank you enough!

359
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:24,800
Shut up!

360
00:22:25,069 --> 00:22:26,700
I didn't do it for the likes of you!

361
00:22:31,584 --> 00:22:32,900
Grand Duke Duralumin!

362
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:35,180
What do you think of this? This is a
medicine that turns things rock-solid!

363
00:22:35,346 --> 00:22:35,720
You fool!

364
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:36,800
Are you trying to make him suffer again?!

365
00:22:37,369 --> 00:22:39,160
We pour this on the prince!

366
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,640
On the prince?

367
00:22:41,940 --> 00:22:42,600
That's right!

368
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:43,073
Grand Duke!

369
00:22:43,259 --> 00:22:47,300
Shedding tears just because he saved us isn't like you at all, Grand Duke!

370
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:49,560
Let's be cold and calculating here!

371
00:22:49,824 --> 00:22:53,640
Unless we get rid of the prince, Prince Plastic can't take the throne!

372
00:22:54,889 --> 00:22:55,889
That's true enough!

373
00:22:58,029 --> 00:22:59,400
Leave everything to me!

374
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:23,680
I just had a dream that you saved me!

375
00:23:23,834 --> 00:23:26,480
Don't dream such silly dreams and get a good night's sleep!

376
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:27,286
Okay!

377
00:23:27,524 --> 00:23:29,826
Now then, I wonder if any kids are staying up late?

378
00:23:29,905 --> 00:23:30,653
Patrol time!

379
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:31,453
Sleep well...

380
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:32,560
For me?

381
00:23:33,409 --> 00:23:34,860
You stay like that for a while!

382
00:24:37,261 --> 00:24:40,881
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

383
